  "route": {
    "description": "Assess the thermodynamic stability of a crystal structure by computing its energy above the convex hull of every structure in Ouro's crystal database: Materials Project, Alexandria and GNoME phases, structures generated on Ouro, and structures submitted earlier. Choose the energy surface: Orb v3 (default), where every reference is scored with the model that scores your structure; PBE, the published DFT energies with your structure scored by Orb v3; or Prophet OAME-MBD, like Orb v3 but with every energy from Prophet (on a GPU; a system's first Prophet hull scores its references). MP2020 corrections are applied on all three. Upload an already-relaxed CIF so the result refers to that geometry; inputs whose max force on an atom or on the cell (stress \u00d7 volume per atom, as ASE's FrechetCellFilter counts it) is over 0.05 eV/\u00c5 are rejected unless `allow_unrelaxed` is set (which relaxes with the surface's model first). A structure the database does not have yet is added to it. Also rejects overlapping-atom CIFs unless `bypass_cif_health_screen` is set. Returns e_above_hull (eV/atom), decomposition products and formation energy; set `include_phase_diagram` for an interactive phase diagram too.",
    "path": "/crystal-db/ehull",
    "method": "POST",
    "parameters": [
